Repository: philippe44/cspot (third_party/cspot), base 60cf17296e2ac9b903e86b92271cb6b4989a80af
Kind:       robustness (crash fix), NOT required to build
Status:     REFERENCE ONLY - the firmware build applies the same change as a source
            overlay (source_overlays.cmake, overlay 3); the submodule stays unmodified.
Check:      git -C third_party/cspot apply --check <this file>

ApResolve::fetchFirstApAddress() dereferences json["ap_list"][0] without
checking that the answer of https://apresolve.spotify.com/ is the expected
JSON. A captive portal, an intercepting proxy, an HTTP error page or an empty
body ends in a NULL pointer access (cJSON build only):

  Guru Meditation Error: Core  1 panic'ed (LoadProhibited). EXCVADDR: 0x00000010
  cspot::ApResolve::fetchFirstApAddress() at ApResolve.cpp:35
  cspot::Session::connectWithRandomAp() at Session.cpp:65

Reproduced in QEMU (ESP-IDF 5.5.5). Throwing instead lets the existing callers
retry: MercurySession::reconnect() catches everything and retries after 5 s.

diff --git a/cspot/src/ApResolve.cpp b/cspot/src/ApResolve.cpp
index 0325150..25edc39 100644
--- a/cspot/src/ApResolve.cpp
+++ b/cspot/src/ApResolve.cpp
@@ -3,6 +3,7 @@
 #include <initializer_list>  // for initializer_list
 #include <map>               // for operator!=, operator==
 #include <memory>            // for allocator, unique_ptr
+#include <stdexcept>         // for runtime_error
 #include <string_view>       // for string_view
 #include <vector>            // for vector
 
@@ -31,8 +32,12 @@ std::string ApResolve::fetchFirstApAddress() {
   // parse json with nlohmann
 #ifdef BELL_ONLY_CJSON
   cJSON* json = cJSON_ParseWithLength(responseStr.data(), responseStr.size());
-  auto ap_string = std::string(
-      cJSON_GetArrayItem(cJSON_GetObjectItem(json, "ap_list"), 0)->valuestring);
+  cJSON* ap = cJSON_GetArrayItem(cJSON_GetObjectItem(json, "ap_list"), 0);
+  if (!cJSON_IsString(ap) || ap->valuestring == nullptr) {
+    cJSON_Delete(json);
+    throw std::runtime_error("apresolve: unexpected response");
+  }
+  auto ap_string = std::string(ap->valuestring);
   cJSON_Delete(json);
   return ap_string;
 #else
